Teach the pinned llama.cpp converter (backend/forks/llama-cpp @ 91f6a6cf) to
convert intfloat/multilingual-e5-small correctly (issue #594, spike S4).

The submodule is NEVER modified: scripts/dev/backend/build_e5_gguf.py copies
the conversion toolchain to a scratch directory and applies this patch there.

Hunk 1 (required): e5 is a BertModel whose tokenizer is the XLM-RoBERTa
SentencePiece (Unigram) one. The stock BertModel.set_vocab takes the
BPE/WordPiece path, which raises on the unknown pre-tokenizer hash -- and
community GGUFs that forced it carry a WordPiece vocab that embeds at cosine
~0.897 of the correct vectors. Routing to _xlmroberta_set_vocab writes the
Unigram vocab; deliberately WITHOUT _xlmroberta_tokenizer_init, because a
BertModel's position ids start at 0 (no RoBERTa pad_token_id+1 offset).

Hunk 2 (recommended): <mask> (id 250001) lives in tokenizer.json's
added_tokens but not in sentencepiece.bpe.model; without this it is written
as [PAD250001] and a text containing a literal "<mask>" tokenizes differently
(measured cosine 0.945/0.970 on two such strings; 0.999999 with the hunk).

With both hunks, tokenization is identical to tokenizer.json on 267/267
corpus texts and 120/120 edge cases (spike S4). Upstream master (2026-11-10)
has the same defect; this patch is a reasonable upstream contribution.

diff --git a/conversion/bert.py b/conversion/bert.py
--- a/conversion/bert.py
+++ b/conversion/bert.py
@@ -38,6 +38,12 @@ class BertModel(TextModel):
             self.gguf_writer.add_classifier_output_labels([v for k, v in sorted(self.cls_out_labels.items())])

     def set_vocab(self):
+        tokenizer_json = self.dir_model / "tokenizer.json"
+        if tokenizer_json.is_file() and json.loads(tokenizer_json.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))["model"]["type"] == "Unigram":
+            # BertModel paired with the XLM-RoBERTa SentencePiece (Unigram) tokenizer,
+            # e.g. intfloat/multilingual-e5-*: write the Unigram vocab, not WordPiece
+            return self._xlmroberta_set_vocab()
+
         tokens, toktypes, tokpre = self.get_vocab_base()
         self.vocab_size = len(tokens)

@@ -224,6 +230,13 @@ class BertModel(TextModel):
                 tokens[250001] = b'<mask>'
                 scores[250001] = 0.0
                 toktypes[250001] = SentencePieceTokenTypes.CONTROL
+            elif (tokenizer_json_path := self.dir_model / "tokenizer.json").is_file():
+                # Add the special tokens tokenizer.json appends after the sentencepiece vocab (e.g. <mask>)
+                for added in json.loads(tokenizer_json_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")).get("added_tokens", []):
+                    if added.get("special") and added["id"] < vocab_size and toktypes[added["id"]] == SentencePieceTokenTypes.UNUSED:
+                        tokens[added["id"]] = added["content"].encode("utf-8")
+                        scores[added["id"]] = 0.0
+                        toktypes[added["id"]] = SentencePieceTokenTypes.CONTROL

         self.gguf_writer.add_tokenizer_model("t5")
         self.gguf_writer.add_tokenizer_pre("default")
